    "title": "Severe Thunderstorm Warning by NWS - NewsBreak",
    "text": "13 minutes ago Check NWS updates here\nEffective: 2025-09-04 00:18:00 EDT Expires: 2025-09-04 00:30:00 EDT Urgency: Immediate Severity: Severe Certainty: Observed Instruction: For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a building. Target Area: Hancock, IN; Henry, IN; Rush, IN At 1218 AM EDT, a severe thunderstorm was located near Greenfield, or 18 miles south of Anderson, moving east at 40 mph.\nHAZARD...60 mph wind gusts.\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\nIMPACT...Expect damage to roofs, siding, and trees.\nLocations impacted include... Greenfield, Knightstown, New Palestine, Carthage, Spiceland, Shirley, Kennard, Wilkinson, and Greensboro.\nThis includes Interstate 70 between mile markers 102 and 121.",
